  "presentation_summary": [
    "Admitted with 2 weeks of high fever around 39 C, generalized rash, muscle weakness, and arthralgia",
    "After 15 days, persistent fever 38-39.5 C despite antibiotics and negative repeat blood cultures",
    "Dermatomyositis features included Gottron sign, diffuse erythema, severe limb weakness, and electromyography consistent with muscle-derived damage",
    "MAS features included cytopenia, ferritin 40000 ng/mL, fibrinogen 0.9 g/L, triglycerides 5.68 mmol/L, splenomegaly, liver dysfunction, coagulopathy, and later CNS symptoms",
    "The patient deteriorated despite high-dose methylprednisolone and died after treatment withdrawal"
  ],
